                <pb facs="0274" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2635: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-15T12:00:00+01:00"
                            >November 15, 1918—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 16—12:15
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2356. My 2347 [<hi rendition="#italic">2346?</hi>].<anchor n="3" xml:id="d113-f1"
                    /> In conversation with Swiss Minister, he said that he has had no instructions
                    from his Government on the subject but Switzerland, he believes, would be
                    willing to take in the small part of the Tyrol known as Vorarlberg, if the
                    population there were substantially unanimous in desiring it, but would not be
                    willing to go beyond this. To take in Tyrol would change completely the
                    character of Switzerland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
